We’d love to hear your feedback on how you’re getting on with ReSharper for Visual Studio Code. What do you like, what’s working for you, and what you’d like to see next. You can let us know in the issue tracker.
And if you’re enjoying ReSharper for Visual Studio Code, don’t forget to leave us a review on the marketplace. Your feedback helps other members of the .NET community make informed decisions and ensures that we continue to improve based on user needs.
